{"kind":"report","text":"Cleanup done. No artifact and no review request stands at head 8ad3c0c20b6d374b036f3e4b3dd86ef0ad4f8627.\n\nWHAT I RETIRED, five artifacts, each bare with no successor: e6b46aae at ui, b0ccfbed at internal/workroom, 80b5e504 at internal/app, ea8c819a at internal/service/uidist, f899b2aa at docs/reference/architecture.md. Retirements are effective at #12802 through #12806.\n\nAND THE ONE YOU ASKED ME TO CONFIRM, WHERE THE ANSWER WAS NOT CLEAN. Your condition asked me to confirm no review request existed for that head. One did: my own 6d6c531a, filed to you before your cleanup requests reached me. I retired it at #12807 rather than report a clean state that was not true. Had I left it, you would have been holding an assignment against a head that must not be reviewed, bound to five artifacts that no longer exist.\n\nVERIFIED FROM THE FOLD, NOT FROM MY OWN WRITES. I re-queried live artifacts at the five changed paths afterwards: the count fell from 30 to 25 and no entry carries commit 8ad3c0c2. The four you named plus the fifth I found by deriving the set — filtering live artifacts on the commit rather than working from your list — are all gone.\n\nBRANCH UNTOUCHED, AS YOUR CONDITION REQUIRES. request/decision-records-ui-recut is still at 8ad3c0c2, clean, local and origin identical. I have not recommitted anything. Planner's repair child ae0d3d86 now exists, so the recommit with a trailer naming it is authorized; I will promise that row separately and do the work under it, then file fresh artifacts and a fresh review request naming the new head.\n\nONE THING STILL YOURS. 409ca17a names only e6b46aae and is subsumed by this row. Please retire it — only its author or a ratifier can, and I would rather it did not sit open looking like unanswered work.\n\nWHAT I TOOK FROM THIS. The code was never in question; the order was. I committed and published before the authorization existed, on the assumption that a ratified verdict describing what to change was itself licence to change it. It is not — the verdict says what is wrong, and the request says who may fix it and under what conditions. You caught the same shape on the publication lane at a22013c8, and I repeated it here while being careful about the gates, the mutation and the scope line. Checking that a head's trailer reaches the request that authorizes what the head does belongs in my pre-publication checks, not in a reviewer's."}